<header><p class="st-kicker">duchy · France and the Low Countries</p><h1 class="st-title">Duchy of Limburg (1839-1867)</h1><p class="st-meta">1839 CE – 1867 CE · capital Maastricht</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The Dutch half of Limburg, made a duchy of the German Confederation in 1839 to compensate the Confederation for losing part of Luxembourg.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-london-1839">Treaty of London</a> of 1839 divided <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/duchy-of-limburg">Limburg</a> between <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kingdom-of-belgium">Belgium</a> and the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kingdom-of-the-netherlands">Netherlands</a>. Because the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/grand-duchy-of-luxembourg">Grand Duchy of Luxembourg</a> lost its western half to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/belgium">Belgium</a>, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch">Dutch</a> part of Limburg was made a duchy and joined the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/german-confederation">German Confederation</a>, held by the Dutch king, though <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maastricht">Maastricht</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/venlo">Venlo</a> were left outside the Confederation.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The duchy was governed as a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch">Dutch</a> province while its estates sent representatives to the Confederation's diet in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/frankfurt">Frankfurt</a>. In 1848 some Limburgers sought separation from the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kingdom-of-the-netherlands">Netherlands</a> to join <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>, and deputies sat in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/frankfurt-parliament">Frankfurt Parliament</a>. Mining and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maastricht">Maastricht's</a> pottery and glass industries developed.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>The <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/german-confederation">German Confederation</a> dissolved after the war of 1866, and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-london-1839">Treaty of London</a> of 1867 confirmed that <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/duchy-of-limburg">Limburg</a> was fully part of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kingdom-of-the-netherlands">Kingdom of the Netherlands</a>. The title 'Duchy of Limburg' lingered in official use until 1906.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/duchy-of-limburg-1839-1867.jpg" alt="Duchy of Limburg (1839-1867)" width="320" height="410"><figcaption>Image: Sir Iain · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Locator_Duchy_of_Limburg_(1350).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1839 CE – 1867 CE</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>duchy</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>bureaucratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Maastricht</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>William II of the Netherlands, William III of the Netherlands</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Catholic Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Dutch and Limburgish</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/netherlands">Netherlands</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Duchy of Limburg (German Confederation)</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1853&amp;focus=duchy-of-limburg-1839-1867" aria-label="Duchy of Limburg (1839-1867) on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4815 420 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Duchy of Limburg (1839-1867) lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5135 676L5110 626M5135 676L5199 691"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5110 626h0M5199 691h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5135 676h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5135 676h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks its recorded location. <a href="/atlas?year=1853&amp;focus=duchy-of-limburg-1839-1867">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

